+/*
+ * The upstream header contributes only the `__percpu_qual` preprocessor
+ * qualifier.  Its generic definition expands to no tokens when an
+ * architecture has not already supplied a qualifier.  Rust has no
+ * corresponding named-address-space qualifier at this source boundary, so
+ * the selected generic fallback has no Rust item or runtime/ABI effect.
+ *
+ * The x86-specific header remains the upstream conditional owner of a
+ * segment-address-space qualifier; this generic fallback neither overrides
+ * nor represents that architecture-specific preprocessor state.
